==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ríkr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*rīkijaz}}, a derivative of {{term/t|gem-pro|*rīks||king, ruler}}, itself a borrowing from {{etyl|cel-pro|is}} {{term/t|cel-pro|*rīxs}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈriːkʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːkʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|ríkari|ríkastur}}

# [[rich]], [[wealthy]]
#: ''Mamma mín er '''rík'''.''
#:: My mom is '''rich'''.
# [[powerful]], [[strong]], [[compelling]]
#: Ég hef '''ríkar''' ástæður.''
#:: I have '''compelling''' reasons.

